  "body": "Sixth production-readiness stage, stacked on PR #53.\n\nThis PR is **calibration-only** with respect to scanner behavior. It does not add adapters, extraction rules, runtime execution, or promotion paths.\n\nCalibration matrix:\n- frozen NotepadNext \u2014 Qt/C++;\n- frozen Moji \u2014 TypeScript/Electron;\n- frozen pell \u2014 plain JavaScript/web;\n- unsupported Python CLI fixture;\n- mixed-language C++/HTML/TypeScript/Python fixture;\n- incomplete metadata-only acquisition;\n- ambiguous static web routing;\n- forced resource-budget interruption.\n\nThe gate runs duplicate cold scans plus the full downstream chain and checks:\n- deterministic canonical rows/projections;\n- zero integrity ERRORs;\n- gaps/challenger/triage count consistency;\n- layered-provenance reconciliation;\n- Blueprint/parity 1:1 contract derivation;\n- portable parity regeneration;\n- unsupported CLI does not invent GUI surfaces;\n- incomplete acquisition remains externally blocked;\n- resource limits remain explicit gaps;\n- ambiguous routing remains uncertain/advisory;\n- scanner runtime contains no calibration specimen-name branches.\n\nObserved counts are recorded but not hand-tuned as pass criteria, avoiding calibration overfitting.\n\nIndependent reconstruction proof remains the next roadmap stage.",
